      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your experience of losing purpose and identity is a profound and painful part of the grieving process, known as destructive guilt or self-questioning. Many people who were their spouse's \"everything\" struggle with this sudden loss of meaning after he is gone, as their entire identity was woven into that care role. Please give yourself permission to feel this emptiness; it does not mean you are nothing, but rather that you are in the early, sharp stages of reconstructing a life where he is still remembered but no longer holds your entire existence.",
